Author: Massimiliano.Pala@p0.f532.n332.z2.fidonet.org


                          X-PWD - Version 2.00
                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This  Program  Just Sets the password in mail packets before them are packed,
useful  if  you  plan  to use XMail!.  Whith this little program, you will be
able to set passwords and be secure about your mail.
	It also Checks the Incoming .pkt files for the right passwords, providing
security check also in Inbound files.
	From  Version 2.00 and Up the program have been compiled for O.S.  2.04+,
ask for 1.3 version!  Or Upgrade your O.S.!!!

Setting it Up:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Just be sure you have the Mail:  assignament to some directory, then copy the
provided configuration file there. The most is done... 
	Now, copy the program to you c:  directory or a dir that is in your path.
Now  it's time to set up the BBS program to use XPwd :  as I currently run E!
this  little  explanation is based on this program, if you find it useful for
other BBS programs, please contact me.
	Go to the XConfig program, then select the 'Site Config' button.  Now for
every  node Listed, you have to re-configure the Packer Command just like the
following :

                        Pwd2 -p "Lha a" <>nil:

Where:

	    -p : is the packing option
	"Lha a": is the packer command to be executed when packing packet files
	  <>nil: redirects output to nil: device

	Ok,  now  select  save  and  go back to main window, select the 'Default'
Button to set the unpacking options.  Edit the 'Unpacker cmd' string as:

                        Pwd2 -I "lha x" %s

	Now  repeat  this  operation  for  every  line dedicated to a packer, the
format  is  ever  the  same,  except  for the packer command ( "lha x" ) that
should be replaced by the appropriate unpacking command ( i.e.  for zip I use
"unzip" ).  Be sure to write in every string the ending %s!
	Ok,  this is All, Remember to edit the .cfg file, ( is Very Simple Indeed
so  I  will  not include any explanation for it, they are included in the cfg
file as comments ) Just some suggestions for it :

1) Remember to use only one line for every command;
2) Add  Every  points  or  Site you are polling from or to,  and the one that
   calls  you;
3) use Full 4D Fidonet Addresses Stile;
4) Do not use passwords longer than 8 char, this is needed because Fidonet
   format expects password to be no more than 8 chars;

	Ok,  This  is  truly the End.  Please if you use this program, just write
some E-Mail to contact me, and give me some suggestion ( if any ), ok???

